From: OpenSourceSDRLab <support@opensourcesdrlab.com>
Subject: [PATCH] XC7Z100-ADRV9371 board support

Board-specific changes to the Analog Devices Linux kernel, branch 2022_R2
(https://github.com/analogdevicesinc/linux, commit
7aa63204d396316bb6c362b34294babae7a6f32b), used for the prebuilt SD-card
image of the OpenSourceSDRLab XC7Z100-ADRV9371:

- ad9371: AD9371 product ID 0x0107, JESD204B framer / deframer lane
  polarity inversion for this board's layout
- adrv9009: SERDES lane polarity inversion (shared ZC706-style DTS base)
- zynq-zc706*.dts(i): board model, PS UART0 console, Ethernet PHY at
  address 0, USB PHY reset on MIO46, W25Q256 QSPI flash partitions,
  ZC706-only I2C/HDMI/audio nodes removed or commented out

Apply with:  git apply 0001-XC7Z100-ADRV9371-board-support.patch
(from the top of the kernel tree). Licence: GPL-2.0, as the files it changes.

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/zynq-zc706-adv7511-adrv9009.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/zynq-zc706-adv7511-adrv9009.dts
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/zynq-zc706-adv7511-adrv9009.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/zynq-zc706-adv7511-adrv9009.dts
@@ -17,23 +17,7 @@
 #include <dt-bindings/gpio/gpio.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/jesd204/adxcvr.h>
 
-&i2c_mux {
-	i2c@5 { /* HPC IIC */
-		#address-cells = <1>;
-		#size-cells = <0>;
-		reg = <5>;
 
-		eeprom@50 {
-			compatible = "at24,24c02";
-			reg = <0x50>;
-		};
-
-		ad7291@2f {
-			compatible = "adi,ad7291";
-			reg = <0x2f>;
-		};
-	};
-};
 
 &fpga_axi {
 	rx_dma: rx-dmac@7c400000 {
